# rvmachine fixtures: freestanding RV64 supervisor guests, flat images entered at 0x80200000 (preload also 0x30 further in, once a test has wrapped it as an ELF).
# Sources are ours (Apache-2.0), in src/; written from the RISC-V privileged and SBI specifications.
#   tiny      firmware console, timer, wfi, serial port, power-off
#   paging    Sv39 turned on through the stvec fault, as a kernel does
#   uclock    user-mode read of the time CSR
#   rfence    one page remapped and made visible by firmware remote-fence calls
#   diskwait  wfi until the block device interrupt or a far timer
#   echo      console input read through the firmware console, then the serial port
#   entropy   forty bytes asked of the virtio entropy device in slot 1, printed as hex
#   ticker    four timed sleeps in wfi, with serial input echoed from the interrupt handler
#   rearm     a timer armed s1 time units ahead and a wfi, in an endless loop
#   masked    serial input against the gates the embedder sets: sie in s3, port enables in s4, controller enables in s5; timed wfi with s2
#   preload   the metadata list of the loader entry (0x30 into the image, a0 = its address) printed record by record, the last module summed and zeroed
#   conport   masked virtio-console binary RX/TX echo; length header and actual driver repost
# Regenerate (authoring time only, no toolchain at test time; LLVM 20 at /usr/lib/llvm-20/bin, OBJ is any scratch dir):
#   for n in tiny paging uclock rfence diskwait echo entropy ticker rearm masked preload conport; do
#     clang --target=riscv64-unknown-elf -march=rv64imafdc -mno-relax -Isrc -c src/$n.S -o $OBJ/$n.o &&
#     ld.lld -N -Ttext=0x80200000 -e _start $OBJ/$n.o -o $OBJ/$n.elf && llvm-objcopy -O binary $OBJ/$n.elf $n.bin; done
